cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "GroundExtract-KR: a value-level truth gate for numbers extracted from Korean regulatory documents"
abstract: >-
  GroundExtract-KR is an open-source verification gate that sits after OCR/LLM
  document extraction. Every extracted number must (1) be grounded verbatim in the
  source text at the span the model cited and (2) satisfy the document domain's
  arithmetic invariants, expressed as YAML rule packs (VAT = supply x 10%,
  assets = liabilities + equity, debit total = credit total). Values that fail
  either check are auto-discarded at confidence 0 before they reach downstream
  systems. The two checks catch disjoint error classes: verbatim grounding catches
  fabricated numbers, while only the arithmetic rules catch a number that is
  genuinely present in the document but attached to the wrong field. The decision
  is made by deterministic code, not by a second model, so it is reproducible and
  runs offline with no API key. The project ships NumHall-KR, a deterministic
  regression suite of 72 documents and 388 labeled fields (64 synthetic from a
  fixed-seed generator plus 8 hand-written), on which the gate reduces the numeric
  hallucination rate from 13.4% to 0.0% at 100% auto-discard recall and 57.8%
  precision, and an MCP server so that agents consume only verified values.
type: software
